DESCRIPTION:Second edition of the Fusion Conferences meeting on redox contr
 ol (ROS\, NAD\, glutathione) in cellular health\, cancer\, ageing\, neurod
 egeneration and cardiometabolic disease. The first edition ran 3-6 Nov 202
 5 in Tulum\, Mexico.\n\nWhy it matters for mTOR (★): Relevance comes fro
 m the attendee list\, not from the programme\, which is exactly what tier 
 3 is for. The announced theme is redox control (ROS\, NAD\, glutathione\, 
 ferroptosis) and mTOR is nowhere in it. What makes this meeting matter to 
 the Atlas is that the published invited-speaker list contains both Brendan
  D. Manning and David M. Sabatini\, the two most heavily represented autho
 rs in the corpus (10 and 46 studies)\, alongside Eileen White and Matthew 
 Vander Heiden. That is the strongest author overlap of any meeting in this
  table. The mechanistic link that does exist runs through oxidative regula
 tion of the TSC complex and the shared metabolite pool supporting anabolis
 m\, but it is inference\, not billed content.\n\nSpeakers or organisers wi
 th a profile in the Atlas: Brendan D. Manning\, David M. Sabatini\n\nConfe
 rence site: https://fusion-conferences.com/conference/211\n\nIn Oliver's m
 TOR Atlas: https://mtor-atlas.org/events/#ev-fusion-2nd-redox-biology-in-h
 ealth-disease-2027
